---
// Figure: four clients adding 1 to one counter, four ways.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
import Readout from '../shared/Readout.astro';
import './clients.css';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="clients-counter" title="Four clients adding 1 to one counter" advance={1000}
  legend={[{ kind: 'client', label: 'Read' }, { kind: 'write', label: 'Write' }, { kind: 'hit', label: 'Reply' }, { kind: 'error', label: 'Transaction refused' }]}
  caption="Illustrative model, slowed down so that each trip across the network takes 0.3 to 0.5 s on screen. Four clients each add 1 to the counter page:views, pause for up to 0.6 s, and add 1 again. Redis executes each command the moment it arrives. With WATCH, a client sends WATCH and GET together, then MULTI, SET and EXEC together. The Lua script reads the counter, adds 1 and writes it back inside Redis. Left out: the time Redis takes to execute anything, and everything else the clients do.">
  <Choice slot="params" name="method" label="Each client adds 1 with" value="getset"
    options={[{ value: 'getset', label: 'GET, then SET' }, { value: 'watch', label: 'WATCH, then a transaction' }, { value: 'incr', label: 'INCR' }, { value: 'script', label: 'a Lua script' }]} />
  <Fragment slot="stats">
    <Readout name="writes" label="Increments Redis executed" kind="write" />
    <Readout name="value" label="Counter shows" kind="redis" />
    <Readout name="lost" label="Increments lost" kind="error" />
    <Readout name="retries" label="Transactions refused" kind="error" />
    <Readout name="trips" label="Round trips per increment" kind="client" />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="counter-scene" data-counter-scene></div>
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>Four clients on the left, Redis on the right holding one counter. Each client's label shows the command it is waiting on; the number above Redis is the counter's value.</p>
    <p>With GET, then SET, two clients often read the same value, say 41, and both write 42: Redis executed two increments and the counter rose by one. After a minute, Redis has executed about 125 increments and the counter shows about 48: most increments were lost, and none of the clients was told. Each increment cost 2 round trips.</p>
    <p>With WATCH, a transaction is refused when another client changed the counter after this one read it, and the client tries again. Nothing is lost, but with four clients competing for one key about three transactions in four are refused, each increment costs about 8 round trips, and after a minute the counter has reached only about 37.</p>
    <p>With INCR, each client sends one command and Redis adds 1 itself. Nothing is lost, each increment costs one round trip, and the clients make about 220 increments in the minute.</p>
    <p>With a Lua script, each client sends one command that reads, adds and writes inside Redis. The result is the same as INCR: nothing lost, nothing refused, one round trip each. The difference is that a script could make any decision between its read and its write.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { mountSim, setReadouts } from '../shared/player.mjs';
  import { createScene } from '../shared/scene.mjs';
  import { create, CLIENTS } from './counter-model.mjs';

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="clients-counter"]').forEach(root => {
    const ids = Array.from({ length: CLIENTS }, (_, i) => `c${i}`);
    const scene = createScene(root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-counter-scene]')!, {
      label: 'Four clients sending commands to one Redis server that holds a counter',
      nodes: [
        ...ids.map((id, i) => ({ id, kind: 'client', label: `Client ${i + 1}` })),
        { id: 'redis', kind: 'redis', label: 'Redis', sublabel: 'page:views' },
      ],
      edges: ids.map(id => ({ id: `${id}-redis`, from: id, to: 'redis' })),
      layout: (width, compact) => {
        const rowH = compact ? 78 : 84, top = 44;
        const positions: Record<string, [number, number]> = {};
        ids.forEach((id, i) => { positions[id] = [compact ? 44 : Math.max(70, width * 0.16), top + i * rowH]; });
        const mid = top + ((CLIENTS - 1) * rowH) / 2;
        positions.redis = [width - (compact ? 52 : Math.max(80, width * 0.18)), mid];
        return { height: top + (CLIENTS - 1) * rowH + 50, positions };
      },
    });

    mountSim(root, {
      seed: 2,
      create: (params: any) => create({ method: params.method }, 2),
      render(model: any) {
        scene.dots(model.movers.active());
        model.clients.forEach((c: any, i: number) => scene.node(`c${i}`).set({ sublabel: c.state }));
        scene.node('redis').set({ badge: String(model.redis.value), badgeKind: 'redis' });
        const s = model.stats;
        const lost = model.lost();
        setReadouts(root, {
          writes: String(s.writes),
          value: String(model.redis.value),
          lost: s.writes ? `${lost} (${Math.round((100 * lost) / s.writes)}%)` : '0',
          retries: String(s.aborted),
          trips: s.writes ? (s.trips / s.writes).toFixed(1) : '–',
        });
        root.dataset.lost = String(lost);
      },
    });
  });
</script>
